        "## 1. My Weekly Workflow Audit\n",
        "\n",
        "I regularly use AI across studying, software development, project work, research, and internship preparation. I classify tasks based on how much human judgment, verification, and responsibility they require.\n",
        "\n",
        "| #  | Recurring task                                                                    | Classification                 | Why                                                                                                                                                                      |\n",
        "| -- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n",
        "| 1  | Studying university subjects and preparing exam notes                             | **Collaborate with AI**        | AI helps me understand difficult concepts, structure notes, and practice questions, but I decide what I need to learn and verify important concepts.                     |\n",
        "| 2  | Solving DSA and programming problems                                              | **Collaborate with AI**        | AI helps me explore approaches, edge cases, and debugging, but I need to understand the algorithm and produce the final solution myself.                                 |\n",
        "| 3  | Debugging programming assignments and project code                                | **Delegate to AI with review** | AI can quickly identify possible bugs and suggest fixes, but I test the changes and verify the underlying reasoning.                                                     |\n",
        "| 4  | Developing and improving my ReviewShieldAI project                                | **Collaborate with AI**        | AI helps with architecture, implementation ideas, debugging, and iteration, while I make the final engineering decisions and verify the implementation.                  |\n",
        "| 5  | Building and improving my portfolio website                                       | **Collaborate with AI**        | AI can accelerate HTML/CSS/JavaScript development and design iterations, but I control the final content, structure, and deployment.                                     |\n",
        "| 6  | Researching unfamiliar technologies, APIs, and development tools                  | **Delegate to AI with review** | AI gives me a fast starting point, but I verify important technical information against reliable or official documentation.                                              |\n",
        "| 7  | Writing project documentation and README files                                    | **Delegate to AI with review** | AI is useful for organizing my technical information into clear documentation, but I verify that the final document accurately represents my project.                    |\n",
        "| 8  | Preparing for technical interviews                                                | **Collaborate with AI**        | AI can simulate interview questions, explain concepts, and critique my answers, while I remain responsible for developing the actual knowledge and communication skills. |\n",
        "| 9  | Preparing internship applications and project descriptions                        | **Delegate to AI with review** | AI can improve clarity and tailor writing to a role, but all experiences, skills, and achievements must come from me.                                                    |\n",
        "| 10 | Drafting professional emails and messages                                         | **Delegate to AI with review** | AI helps me make communication clearer and more professional, but I decide what I actually want to communicate.                                                          |\n",
        "| 11 | Completing an examination or assessment where outside assistance is not permitted | **Just me**                    | The result needs to represent my own knowledge, reasoning, and performance, so I should not delegate the work to AI.                                                     |\n",
        "| 12 | Making final decisions about my career direction and major project choices        | **Just me**                    | AI can provide perspectives and trade-offs, but these decisions involve my own priorities, responsibilities, and long-term goals.                                        |\n",
        "\n",
        "### What I learned from the audit\n",
        "\n",
        "The audit shows that I do not want to treat AI as a replacement for my own judgment. The most useful pattern for me is **collaboration with verification**: AI can accelerate research, coding, writing, and learning, but I remain responsible for deciding what is correct and whether the final result meets my requirements.\n",
        "\n",
        "I also identified two areas that should remain primarily human-owned: assessments where outside assistance is not allowed and personal career/project decisions.\n",
        "\n",
